    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# n8n Workflow Overview: Stock Analysis Automation\n\nThis document provides a detailed overview of the n8n workflow designed to automate stock analysis, delivering technical chart analysis and insights through Telegram and scheduled processes.\n\n## Workflow Components\n\n### Telegram Trigger\n- Initiates the workflow by receiving user messages or voice inputs via Telegram.\n- Supports text-based requests or voice transcription for stock analysis.\n\n### Webhook\n- Handles external HTTP POST requests to trigger stock analysis programmatically.\n- Processes incoming data to extract text for analysis.\n\n### Switch\n- Routes incoming Telegram messages based on input type (voice or text).\n- Directs voice messages to transcription and text messages to processing.\n\n### Download File\n- Retrieves voice message files from Telegram for transcription.\n- Prepares audio data for further processing.\n\n### Transcribe\n- Utilizes OpenAI's transcription service to convert voice messages into text.\n- Integrates transcribed text into the analysis workflow.\n\n### Set Text\n- Extracts and sets text from Telegram messages or webhook inputs.\n- Prepares user queries for AI-driven analysis.\n\n### AI Agent\n- Core component powered by OpenAI's GPT-4o model, specializing in stock analysis.\n- Processes user requests, interacts with tools, and generates conversational responses.\n- Maintains a professional tone and avoids direct financial recommendations.\n- Uses Window Buffer Memory to retain context across interactions.\n\n### Window Buffer Memory\n- Stores conversation history to provide context-aware responses.\n- Enhances the AI Agent's ability to maintain coherent interactions.\n\n### Get Chart\n- Calls a sub-workflow to generate stock charts based on user-specified ticker and chart style (e.g., candle, bar, line).\n- Defaults to \"candle\" style if not specified.\n- Returns chart URLs in markdown format for inclusion in responses.\n\n### Workflow Input Trigger\n- Accepts ticker and chart style inputs for chart generation.\n- Initiates the chart creation process.\n\n### Set Values\n- Assigns ticker and chart style values from user inputs or AI Agent outputs.\n- Ensures accurate data for chart generation.\n\n### Get Chart URL\n- Sends a POST request to the chart API to generate a stock chart.\n- Configures chart parameters, including style, theme, interval (1-week), and technical indicators (Volume, RSI, Stochastic RSI).\n- Returns the chart URL for further processing.\n\n### Download Chart\n- Downloads the generated chart image from the provided URL.\n- Prepares the chart for technical analysis.\n\n### Technical Analysis\n- Analyzes stock charts using OpenAI's GPT-4o model.\n- Evaluates candlestick patterns, RSI, Stochastic RSI, trading volume, and market sentiment.\n- Provides detailed insights, including:\n  - Candlestick pattern interpretation (e.g., bullish engulfing, doji).\n  - RSI value and market positioning (overbought, oversold, neutral).\n  - Stochastic RSI K and D line analysis, including crossovers and divergences.\n- Delivers clear, data-driven conclusions for informed decision-making.\n\n### Send Chart\n- Sends the generated chart to the user via Telegram as a photo.\n- Ensures seamless delivery of visual data.\n\n### Send Analysis\n- Delivers the AI Agent's textual analysis and insights to the user via Telegram.\n- Includes markdown-formatted chart URLs and conversational explanations.\n\n### Save Ticker\n- Stores user-specified tickers in an Airtable database for future reports.\n- Triggered when users request to save a ticker for recurring analysis.\n\n### Schedule Trigger\n- Initiates scheduled stock analysis for predefined tickers.\n- Runs at specified intervals to automate recurring reports.\n\n### Get Tokens\n- Retrieves saved tickers from the Airtable database.\n- Provides input for scheduled analysis loops.\n\n### Loop Over Items\n- Iterates over retrieved tickers to generate individual stock analyses.\n- Supports batch processing for multiple tickers.\n\n### Run Agent\n- Sends HTTP POST requests to the webhook for each ticker in the scheduled loop.\n- Triggers AI Agent analysis for each stock.\n\n## Workflow Scenarios\n\n### Scenario 1: AI Agent Interaction\n- Users interact via Telegram, sending text or voice requests for stock analysis.\n- The AI Agent processes requests, generates charts, and delivers technical insights.\n- Charts and analyses are sent back to the user via Telegram.\n\n### Scenario 2: Scheduled Analyses\n- Automatically analyzes predefined tickers stored in Airtable on a set schedule.\n- Generates and sends reports for each ticker without user intervention.\n\n## Key Features\n- **Conversational Analysis**: Provides clear, user-friendly explanations of complex financial data.\n- **Technical Depth**: Includes detailed analysis of candlestick patterns, RSI, Stochastic RSI, and volume.\n- **Flexible Inputs**: Supports text, voice, and scheduled triggers for versatile use cases.\n- **Scalability**: Handles multiple tickers through looping and batch processing.\n- **Data Persistence**: Saves tickers in Airtable for recurring analysis.\n\nThis workflow combines AI-driven insights, automated chart generation, and seamless Telegram integration to deliver a robust solution for stock analysis.\n",
        "height": 3040,
        "width": 820,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
